<template><main id="main" class="shell member-page"><h1>How this local edition works</h1><p>Every available story is an original fictional demonstration. Source names, events and example-domain links are fictional. Simulated fixture approvals are not real editorial verification.</p><h2>Sources are evidence, not scores</h2><NuxtLink to="/sources">Browse the actual fictional source directory</NuxtLink><p>Each article keeps its complete numbered bibliography and claim-linked citations. Source availability, corrections and exact item links remain visible. Unknown permission denies use. Context-only links do not satisfy the evidence threshold.</p><h2>Private engine work stays private</h2><p>The offline source-to-draft engine produces unpublished extractive drafts. They are not this reader catalogue, and cannot be promoted here without later review and publication controls.</p><h2>Your edition</h2><p>For you uses only explicit follows, mutes and hidden stories. Team and competition interests are different. No passive reading profile is inferred. Empty coverage remains empty.</p><h2>Original media</h2><p>Radio and Clips use local synthetic voices. Newsroom uses original animated presenters. These are not real recordings of events or photorealistic people. Eligibility is checked again when media is requested.</p><NuxtLink to="/search">Browse fictional stories and their sources</NuxtLink></main></template>
